        {
          "id": "64e0a6350568d84b9868a9ab",
          "questionNumber": 1,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "Which of the following branch is not located to the south-east or north-east of branch O?",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "G",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "S",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "F",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "U",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "L",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "2",
          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Now, as per the given information in the question we get the following direction diagrams:</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">1. F is 12 km to the west of G. U is situated exactly in the middle of F and G. Combining these two statements, we get-</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/09/F1_Banking_Arbaz_7-9-23_D9.png\" style=\"width: 416px; height: 324px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">2. U is 7 km to the south of S. S is 12 km to the east of O. Combining these two statements we get-</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/09/F1_Banking_Arbaz_7-9-23_D10.png\" style=\"height: 324px; width: 416px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">3. L is 7 km to the north of H. O is 6 km to the west of H. Combining these two statements we get the final direction diagram as follows-</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/09/F1_Banking_Arbaz_7-9-23_D11.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); height: 324px; width: 416px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">From the above direction diagram, we see that branches F, U and G are located to the south-east of O and branch L is located to the north-east of O.</p>\n\n<p>Hence, <strong>branch S is not located to the south-east or north-east of branch O</strong>.&nbsp;</p>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
        {
          "id": "64e0a6350568d84b9868a9ac",
          "questionNumber": 2,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "The ratio of the distance between branch L and branch F to the distance between branch U and branch G is?",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "3:7",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "1:2",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "6:7",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "7:3",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "3:2",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "4",
          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Now, as per the given information in the question we get the following direction diagrams:</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">1. F is 12 km to the west of G. U is situated exactly in the middle of F and G. Combining these two statements, we get-</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/09/F1_Banking_Arbaz_7-9-23_D9.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); width: 416px; height: 324px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">2. U is 7 km to the south of S. S is 12 km to the east of O. Combining these two statements we get-</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/09/F1_Banking_Arbaz_7-9-23_D10.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); height: 324px; width: 416px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">3. L is 7 km to the north of H. O is 6 km to the west of H. Combining these two statements we get the final direction diagram as follows-</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/09/F1_Banking_Arbaz_7-9-23_D11.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); height: 324px; width: 416px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>From the above direction diagram, we see that-</p>\n\n<p>The distance between branch L and branch F is = 7+7 = 14 km</p>\n\n<p>The distance between branch U and branch G is= 6 km</p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the ratio between the two distances is 14 km: 6 km.</p>\n\n<p>Hence, <strong>the required ratio between the two distances is 7:3</strong>.&nbsp;</p>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
        {
          "id": "64e0a6350568d84b9868a9ad",
          "questionNumber": 3,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements is/are not false?</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement I</strong>: Branch L is located to the north-west of branch U.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement II</strong>: Branch H is situated exactly in the middle of branch O and branch S.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement III</strong>: Branch G is located to the north-east of branch S.&nbsp;</p>",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "Only Statement I",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "Both Statements I and II",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "None of the above",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "Only Statement III",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "Both statements II and III",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "2",
          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p>Now, as per the given information in the question we get the following direction diagrams:</p>\n\n<p>1. F is 12 km to the west of G. U is situated exactly in the middle of F and G. Combining these two statements, we get-</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/09/F1_Banking_Arbaz_7-9-23_D9.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); width: 416px; height: 324px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>2. U is 7 km to the south of S. S is 12 km to the east of O. Combining these two statements we get-</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/09/F1_Banking_Arbaz_7-9-23_D10.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); height: 324px; width: 416px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>3. L is 7 km to the north of H. O is 6 km to the west of H. Combining these two statements we get the final direction diagram as follows-</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/09/F1_Banking_Arbaz_7-9-23_D11.png\" style=\"height: 324px; width: 416px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>From the above direction diagram, we check the correctness of the given statements as follows:</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement I</strong> states that branch L is located to the north-west of branch U. This statement is <strong><em>true</em></strong>.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement II</strong> states branch H is situated exactly in the middle of branch O and branch S. This statement is <strong><em>true</em></strong>. &nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement III</strong> states that branch G is located to the north-east of branch S. This statement is <strong><em>false</em></strong>.</p>\n\n<p>Hence, <strong>both Statements I and II are not false</strong>.&nbsp;</p>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
